From: OpenWrt R18 port
Subject: PCI: mediatek: don't retrain ports limited to Gen1

EN7528 RC0 has a Gen1-only PHY. Retraining it when a Gen2-capable
endpoint is attached (MT7915 second host interface, 14c3:7916) leaves the
link up and config space working, but every MMIO read to the endpoint
then stalls the bus and hangs the SoC. Stock firmware only retrains RC1.

Skip mtk_pcie_retrain() for ports whose device tree node limits them to
Gen1 with the standard max-link-speed property.

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek.c
@@ -1317,7 +1317,8 @@ static int mtk_pcie_probe(struct platfor
 	 * Ignore error because pci_host_probe() was already called, and in any
 	 * case it is possible that the port will still work as Gen1.
 	 */
-	if (pcie->soc->quirks & MTK_PCIE_RETRAIN)
+	if ((pcie->soc->quirks & MTK_PCIE_RETRAIN) &&
+	    of_pci_get_max_link_speed(dev->of_node) != 1)
 		mtk_pcie_retrain(dev, host);
 
 	return 0;
